{
 "subtitle": "10 finished runs, 1.1M env steps each, size50m, one training seed per run. Scored with tools/death_eval.py on the same fixed evaluation worlds. Updated 2026-10-03.",
 "summary": "Every number is the mean episode-final achievement count over the evaluation episodes, and each unlock rate is the share of episodes in which that achievement fired. Every run was scored on the same fixed evaluation worlds; re-scoring two old checkpoints with today's code reproduced them exactly.\nExperiment B sets the record. Masking impossible actions during training (B2) reaches 7.60 achievements, against 5.87 for the same model without it; giving the agent the validity flags as an input (B1) reaches 6.90. The furnace, never placed in any earlier run despite hundreds of chances, is placed in 40% of B2's episodes; it also places stone (40%), mines coal (20%) and, for the first time, makes and places a torch (3%).\nThe non-cheating model (Honest map) matches the privileged control (5.87 vs 5.93), so dropping privileged supervision cost nothing measurable.\nEvery map run except the hand-written-rewards one unlocks WAKE_UP (sleep, then wake) in 80-98% of episodes; vanilla never does. Without it the map model alone scores 4.20 against vanilla's 4.44; the gains that remain come from the potential and from experiment B (B2 6.80, B1 6.10 without WAKE_UP).\nSurvival is still unsolved: lifespans 243-311 steps against 261-284 for a random policy. In normalized return the best run is about 3.0% of the 226-point maximum, against roughly 7% reported for the state of the art.",
 "table_note": "eps = evaluation episodes. ach. = mean episode-final achievements; w/o wake = the same minus WAKE_UP. life = mean lifespan in steps. Rates are % of episodes. 'bug' = imag_shift True, which corrupted the policy gradient (fixed 2026-09-20). map_survive was re-evaluated on 2026-09-28 and reproduced its original 2.30. One training seed per run, so the run-to-run spread is unknown. 'Map + potential (fixed)' is the old 5.80 record; 'Control' adds the recipe and death fixes with the privileged map; 'Honest map' has the same fixes with observation-only targets. 'B1' and 'B2' are experiment B on the honest-map configuration: validity flags as an encoder input, and impossible actions masked in training.",
